---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import SecretsScrubber from '@/components/tools/redact/text/SecretsScrubber.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="secrets-scrubber" width="wide">
  <SecretsScrubber client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to scrub secrets from logs and code</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Paste a log, a stack trace, a config file or code, or drop the file on the box.</li>
      <li>The secrets scrubber replaces each secret value at once. Line breaks, keys and timestamps stay as they were.</li>
      <li>Check the findings list for the line number and type of each value.</li>
      <li>Press a mark in the result to keep a value that is not secret.</li>
      <li>Copy the result or download it with the same file extension.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the secrets scrubber finds</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keys and tokens of more than 60 providers by their known prefix and length: cloud platforms, code hosting, package registries, payment providers, AI APIs, chat webhooks and more.</li>
      <li>Private key blocks, JSON web tokens, and tokens in Authorization, API key and Cookie headers.</li>
      <li>Passwords in connection strings such as postgres://user:password@host, and values of config keys that end in password, secret, token, api_key or similar.</li>
      <li>Long random strings, by their entropy and their mix of letters and digits. Commit hashes, checksums, UUIDs and package integrity values are not flagged.</li>
      <li>Optional: email addresses, IP and MAC addresses, and internal host names such as db01.corp or *.svc.cluster.local.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Only pattern rules, in the page. There is no model to download, and a 1 MB log takes about one second. Logs over
      40,000 characters are scanned in a background thread so the page does not freeze.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open the Network tab in your browser's developer tools and paste your log. The page makes no request. You can also
      load the page, turn off your network and use it.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A secret with no known format and no telling key name, such as a short password in a sentence, is not found. Check the result by eye.</li>
      <li>If a key was ever shared, committed or pasted into a chat, rotate it. Scrubbing protects the next copy only.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
